# Confirm before changing files (G3)

Before creating, renaming, moving, or editing **any** file in `fe/`, `be/`, or the repo root, **stop**. Do not write, delete, or run mutating git commands yet.

Read-only exploration (read, search, git status) is allowed so the list is accurate.

## What to post

A numbered list of **every** intended change:

- **Create** — full path and what it is
- **Modify** — full path and what will change
- **Delete** — full path and why
- **Git** — branch to create/switch to, if any

Do not start implementing in the same turn. Wait for an explicit go-ahead such as: yes, confirmed, go ahead, execute, do it, proceed, ok.

After confirmation, execute **only** what was listed. If the plan changes, post an updated list and wait again.

This gate applies even for small edits. It does not apply to answering questions with no file changes.
